    <div class="itdgl-clinic-intro">
      <p>Choosing a marketing agency for a dermatology clinic in Dombivli, Maharashtra is different from choosing one for a D2C brand or a restaurant. Dermatologists face specific challenges: ASCI medical-advertising code + Maharashtra Medical Council norms restrict claims, before-after content needs compliance-safe framing, patient reviews require consent, and Google Business Profile competition in Dombivli East + Dombivli West + MIDC + Kopar is dense with 50+ dermatology + hair-transplant clinics in Dombivli + immediate suburbs. This FAQ answers 12 questions Dombivli dermatologists ask about hiring a full-service marketing agency.</p><p>Consultation fee context in Dombivli: Rs 400-1,200 dermatology, Rs 600-1,800 trichology, Rs 800-2,500 hair transplant initial consultation. Hero procedures: HydraFacial + laser hair reduction + acne + hair PRP + hair transplant (fewer clinics offering advanced FUE).</p>
    </div>

    <div class="itdgl-evidence-band">
      <strong>ITD CLINIC MARKETING &mdash; WHAT WE ACTUALLY DO:</strong>
      ITD GrowthLabs runs full-stack digital marketing for dermatology + skincare clinics across Thane, Mumbai, Navi Mumbai, Dombivli, Kalyan, Nagpur, Nashik, and Pune. Social media management + Reels + viral content, Meta + Google ads, website + online booking + WhatsApp Cloud API integration, Google Business Profile optimisation + local SEO, and patient lead generation. We work with clinics that don't have in-house marketing teams — treating the marketing function as an outsourced growth partner, not a vendor. Every answer below reflects live clinic work.
    </div>

    <div class="itdgl-faq-list" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How to choose a marketing agency for a dermatology clinic in Dombivli?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Ten-point framework: (1) Named dermatology / medical clinic client work with verifiable case studies + live URLs. (2) ASCI medical-advertising code + Maharashtra Medical Council compliance familiarity. (3) Before-after content methodology (same lighting + angle + time + patient consent + disclaimer). (4) GMB + local SEO expertise for Dombivli — Lower GMB competition than Thane/Mumbai — 30-40 clinics ranked in Dombivli pincode. Big opportunity for GMB dominance for early-mover clinics. (5) WhatsApp Cloud API + booking integration. (6) Reels + short-form video production capacity (in-house or partner). (7) Ad-spend transparency (no markup — client sees platform invoice). (8) Reporting cadence (weekly performance + monthly QBR). (9) Founder + senior access. (10) Contract terms — 6-month MSA with cancellation after month 3, 100% client IP on creative + booking system + patient data.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What is a realistic monthly retainer for a dermatology clinic in Dombivli?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Retainer range: Rs 25,000-1.5 lakh. Starter (Rs 35-60K/month Dombivli) suits solo dermatologist clinics with Rs 3-8 lakh/month revenue and 60-150 new patients/month target — includes GMB + basic social + 1 paid channel. Growth (Rs 80K-1.8L/month Dombivli) suits 2-3 doctor clinics with Rs 10-40 lakh/month revenue — full-stack social + Reels + Meta + Google + WhatsApp + GMB. Enterprise (Rs 2-4L/month Dombivli) suits multi-location or chain clinics Rs 40 lakh+/month — adds premium creative + celebrity + PR + video + expanded team. Ad spend separate + transparent pass-through: Rs 30,000-2.5 lakh.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What compliance do marketing agencies need to know for dermatology in Dombivli?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Maharashtra Medical Council + MCI Code of Ethics Regulation 6.1 (advertising restrictions on doctors), ASCI medical advertising code (no guarantee of cure, no comparative claims, no before-after without qualifications), Drugs and Magic Remedies Act (prohibits ads claiming to cure certain conditions), Consumer Protection Act (misleading claims). Compliant approach: education-first content (condition explainers + procedure info), compliance-safe before-after (same lighting + angle + time + patient consent + individual-results-may-vary disclaimer), patient testimonials with written consent form, no guaranteed outcome language. In Dombivli, Maharashtra Medical Council + Maharashtra FDA + KDMC (Kalyan-Dombivli Municipal Corporation) enforcement.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What named dermatology client work should a marketing agency show?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Verifiable evidence: (1) Live URLs of dermatology clinic Instagram + Facebook + Google Business Profile with GMB rank screenshots for Dombivli pincode area, (2) 2-3 named client references (available on discovery call under NDA), (3) case study PDFs with real metrics (patient inquiries/month, cost per lead, booking conversion, revenue attribution), (4) content library samples (compliance-safe before-after + Reels + educational carousels). Red flag: 'we've worked with 50+ clinics' with no named client work + no verifiable URLs = category tourism.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What contract terms + exit clauses should dermatology clinics negotiate with a marketing agency?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">6-month MSA (Master Service Agreement) with cancellation option after month 3 if agreed milestones not met — protects both sides. Monthly retainer + performance milestones defined upfront. Ad-spend transparent pass-through — client pays platforms directly OR agency bills exactly platform-invoice amount. NO ad-spend markup. IP ownership 100% client on: creative assets, content library, GMB access, WhatsApp automation, website, booking system, ALL patient data. Notice period 30-60 days. Non-solicitation clause reasonable. Avoid: 12-24 month lock-ins, IP-retention clauses, ad-spend markup, unclear termination terms, patient-data-retention by agency.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What team structure will a dermatology marketing agency assign to a Dombivli clinic?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Growth-tier pod typical: (1) Account Director / Growth Lead — weekly review + monthly QBR + strategy + compliance oversight. (2) Performance marketer — Meta + Google ads + GMB + landing pages. (3) Creative pod — designer + video editor + Reels producer (8-15 pieces/month). (4) Social media manager — Instagram + Facebook + community management + DMs + WhatsApp handoff. (5) Content writer — educational carousels + captions + email + WhatsApp templates. (6) Local SEO + GMB specialist — reviews + posts + Q&amp;A + citations. Founder + senior partner on quarterly QBR.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What reporting cadence to expect from a dermatology marketing agency?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Weekly performance snapshot (Monday for previous week): patient inquiries + cost per lead + GMB rank + Reels reach + WhatsApp DMs + booking conversion. Monthly QBR (in-person for Dombivli local + video for remote): full P&amp;L + cohort analysis + creative + channel review + next month plan + quarterly forecast. Quarterly business review: revenue against plan + tier + team + compliance audit + next quarter strategy. Compliance review monthly (any ASCI risk in content).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">In-house marketing team vs agency vs hybrid for a Dombivli dermatology clinic?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">In-house makes sense at Rs 60 lakh+/month clinic revenue when team is 3-4 specialists (Social + Performance + GMB + Video). Full agency for Rs 3 lakh-60 lakh/month clinic revenue — access to specialist expertise + creative + tooling + compliance advisory without hiring overhead. Hybrid (Rs 30-60 lakh/month) — in-house marketing manager + specialist agency execution for creative + performance + GMB. In Dombivli, most solo + 2-3 doctor practices operate best with full agency; multi-location chains with hybrid model. ITD positions specifically for clinics that don't have in-house marketing teams — treating marketing as an outsourced growth partner.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What are red flags in dermatology marketing agency proposals?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">(1) 'Industries served 20+' category tourism with no medical/clinic depth. (2) Guaranteed leads or ROAS promises (unrealistic + ASCI-risky). (3) Bundled ad-spend + retainer (hides 15-30% markup). (4) 12-24 month lock-ins with no cancellation clause. (5) IP-retention clauses on creative + booking + patient data. (6) Junior-only team, no founder access. (7) No named clinic client work + no verifiable URLs. (8) Can't answer basic ASCI medical-advertising code questions. (9) No before-after compliance methodology. (10) Uses generic beauty-brand content templates instead of medical + educational content.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What is a realistic first-90-day plan from a dermatology marketing agency in Dombivli?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Month 1 — Audit + Foundation: current GMB + Instagram + website audit, baseline patient-inquiry benchmarking, ASCI compliance review of existing content, creative pipeline design (10-15 Reels + carousels), WhatsApp Cloud API setup, GMB optimisation, first landing page live. Month 2 — Launch + Iterate: paid campaigns live (Meta + Google + GMB posts), creative testing + weekly optimisation, review generation programme, first cohort measurement. Month 3 — Optimise + First QBR: channel + creative + audience optimisation, first quarterly QBR + 90-day performance review, tier recalibration, quarter-2 plan. Go/no-go milestones at day 30, 60, 90. Cancellation clause after month 3.</div>
